$b['A towering Gothic cathedral structure built vertically from pointed arches narrow columns and black tracery tapering naturally as it descends'] = 'Two panels side by side on one image, divided down the middle. LEFT PANEL: the tattoo design alone on a plain white background, shown flat exactly as described, no body, drawn large so it fills most of the panel. RIGHT PANEL: Studio photograph of a real person''s body showing the same exact tattoo where described, healed tattoo on real skin in soft even light, the rest of the body modestly covered by simple plain clothing, only the tattooed area bare, plain seamless light grey studio backdrop - no room, no furniture, no scenery. The tattoo in both panels is identical. The tattoo: A towering Gothic cathedral structure built vertically from pointed arches, narrow columns and black tracery, tapering naturally as it descends. Monumental, Gothic, sacred. In the right panel it is on a man, full spine from upper back toward lower back. Create exceptional contemporary Dark Ornamental tattoo artwork designed specifically around human anatomy. DARK ORNAMENTAL = THE BODY DECORATED WITH DARK STRUCTURE. The ornament itself may be the entire subject. Draw from: Gothic architecture Cathedral tracery Pointed arches Wrought iron Dark jewelry Filigree Lace Thorns Blades Spikes Chains Botanical structures Sacred geometry Historical ornament Medieval engraving Woodcut textures Negative space Heavy blackwork Architectural repetition Do not automatically include: Skulls Faces Animals Demons Flowers Eyes Literal Gothic objects They may appear when conceptually appropriate, but Dark Ornamental does not require a conventional central subject. Avoid making 100 versions of the same symmetrical sternum tattoo. Vary: Scale Density Line weight Black coverage Symmetry Asymmetry Historical influence Body location Movement Negative space Gender presentation Composition Some pieces should be extremely fine. Some should be brutally heavy. Some should r